<title>BRAZIL: SOCCER-GREMIO WIN BRAZILIAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-GREMIO WIN BRAZILIAN CHAMPIONSHIP.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-12-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gremio beat Portuguesa 2-0 (halftime 1-0) in the second leg of the Brazilian championship final on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers: Paulo Nunes (3), Ailton (85)</p>
<p>Attendance: 55,000</p>
<p>Aggregate score 2-2. Gremio win the title by having the better overall record in the competition.</p>
</text>
